"<strong>How far it works.</strong> Every instrument can place a star only to within some small angle, its position uncertainty. When the parallax is not much bigger than that, the distance is poorly known. The share of the distance that is uncertain equals the share of the parallax that is uncertain: (uncertainty in p) ÷ p.",
